  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Shelter Assistance in Badakhshan Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Frequent natural hazards (including earthquakes, floods, and landslides) have left many families without adequate shelter, exacerbating their already vulnerable living conditions in Badakhshan province in Afghanistan. Since the first earthquake incident earlier in October 2023, families affected by earthquake in Afghanistan are in need of emergency shelter assistance. 
 
In this project, IOM ensures the continuity of shelter interventions for vulnerable families, host community and internally displaced persons (IDPs) and addresses their shelter needs in Badakhshan province while integrating protection principles throughout the response. This project focuses on repairing and improving damaged shelters, ensuring that individuals have safe and adequate housing.</narrative>
  </description>
